            text: "A thump that keeps time with your footstrike and disappears with the belt running empty is structural. The usual causes are loose deck mounting bolts, hardened or missing deck cushions, a loose frame or folding joint, or a levelling foot that is not touching the floor so the frame rocks on every step.",
